Just to add my $.02 to this. I think if someone wants to savescum on
their own system they can do it all they like, as long as they don't
claim any ascensions as a legitimate win. But I do believe that it is
not the best or the most rewarding way to learn.

When I first started playing Nethack in '93, I did savescum. This was
partially because I was new to roguelike games and the concept of a
game where you couldn't return to a save point was alien to me, and
partly because the person who introduced me to the game (who later
became my first husband) savescummed himself. Despite savescumming and
reading spoilers - then downloaded in Word format from a BBS as this
was pre-WWW - it took me quite awhile to "win", and I was not at all
satisfied until I won for real, without using backed-up save files.
After that first legitimate win, which came after about a year of
playing, I never savescummed again, and only backed up save files as
the restore feature on the Mac port of the program was not that
reliable.

Since last January I've played exclusively on NAO, so there is no
possibility of savescumming even if I were tempted to do so. I like
that this evens the playing field, so people's ascensions on this and
other public servers can be compared fairly.

For the record, my now-ex-husband who savescummed never did ascend, at
least not while we were still married. He said it was because he
always got bored with the game. I said maybe if he didn't savescum he
wouldn't - oh well, to each his own...

